  "question": {
    "text": "A storage tower supplies water, as shown in the figure. If&nbsp;&nbsp;<math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></math> is the atmospheric pressure<br />\r<br />\r<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>h</mi></math>= height of water level,&nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>g&nbsp;</mi></math>= acceleration due to gravity,&nbsp;&nbsp;<math><mi>ρ</mi><mo>=</mo></math> density and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>v</mi></math>= velocity of flow in the horizontal pipe at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math>, then the pressure at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math>&nbsp;is -<br />\r<br />\r<img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/golillu.PNG\" style=\"width: 270px; height: 270px;\" />",
    "image": null
  },
